# Source selection and ambient residual reductions for 13.6.23

The actual W_K quotient makes the K⁺ component action faithful. A marked
source parabolic and an outside Tᵥ actor then give dimension four and the
middle node. The literal Y_z criterion uses 13.6.16(3) and inherits movement
from Lᵥ. Genuine 1.2.4 supplies a containing C-component K₊, normal in Gᵥ.
The comparison of the actual intrinsic SL₄(2) quotients identifies K with
this component, and the proved centerless A.3.18 argument gives
prime-to-three index and the exact ambient prime-to-three residual equality.

`source_rankFour_selection` assembles these conclusions from the genuine
earlier-source contract. It constructs the parabolic marking, excludes the
inner-action branch, and proves the intrinsic markings through the literal
action kernels. It also exhibits an actual Tᵥ⁺ actor inducing the graph
automorphism modulo inner automorphisms. No clause of 13.6.23 is assumed.
The explicit earlier 13.6.2–22 and universal A.3 inputs retain their source
owners; the orthogonal-module and Thompson endgame remain with the parent.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.6.23, printed p.933/PDF p.950.
-/
